# DK Industry pilot graph

This rule permits only read-only queries of the existing pilot graph. It does not
authorize extraction, update, merge, integration installation, watch mode, hooks,
Cloud, MCP, semantic processing, or data upload without a separate explicit request.

Executable:

`C:\Users\LOQ\.local\bin\graphify.exe`

Approved graph:

`C:\Autumn2026\CTDK\dk-industry\.tmp\graphify-pilot\combined.json`

Example of a permitted query using an exact node ID:

```powershell
$env:GRAPHIFY_BACKEND = 'none'
$env:GRAPHIFY_QUERY_LOG_DISABLE = '1'
& 'C:\Users\LOQ\.local\bin\graphify.exe' explain `
  'backend::models_quotation' `
  --graph 'C:\Autumn2026\CTDK\dk-industry\.tmp\graphify-pilot\combined.json'
```

Set both environment variables immediately before every Graphify invocation.
Pass the approved graph path explicitly to each graph-reading command that
supports `--graph`.

## Freshness

Git cleanliness and file mtimes are not sufficient evidence of freshness. This
pilot has no retained extraction-time snapshot or hash set covering every source
and resolution input. Unless such a comparison is available, mark freshness as
unverified and inspect the directly relevant current source before concluding.
Include tracked, untracked, and uncommitted changes in any freshness review.

## Graph semantics and query discipline

`combined.json` was normalized into an undirected simple graph during merge. Do
not use edge direction, `affected`, or `path` results from this graph to assert
dependency direction or complete impact without checking source or the relevant
original per-corpus graph.

Prefer exact node IDs when symbols share a name. If output is truncated, narrow
the symbol, relation, corpus, or depth; do not infer from omitted results. Verify
important edges against their source file, source location, target node ID, and
current source.

## Verified coverage and limits

Coverage is limited to the examples inspected during the pilot:

- One frontend TypeScript alias import resolved correctly.
- Selected backend route-to-model and route-to-service imports resolved correctly.
- Imports from `backend/test` into `backend/src` remained external placeholders.

Do not generalize these observations to every internal dependency. Parent
resolution configs are outside the corpus manifests. `auth.test.js` and
`runtime.test.js` were excluded. The graph covers only `frontend/src`,
`backend/src`, and the filtered `backend/test` corpus.

No application workflow was verified at runtime. Use `rg`, LSP, current source,
and appropriate tests for correctness, authorization, transactions, rollback,
concurrency, expiry races, partial writes, duplicate-key behavior, notifications,
realtime delivery, and end-to-end behavior. These are unverified risks, not
reproduced bugs.
